 "text": "Hello, how are you today? Find a breezy spot that the wind isn't about to change. Split the wood into chunks first, it helps a lot. Yes, and you can make them right at camp. A tight pile of them gives you lot more fire fast. I did. They keep the bugs off your face and the fire burning. It should be big enough to heat your tea, or bacon if you' lucky. Then a small fire is enough. Build it in a ring, so the fire can't catch the ground on you. Make sure it' out cold, and cover it with dirt. Then water the whole thing, it makes sure it didn't start again.",
